<title>USA: Clinton transfers Hong Kong trade offices to China.</title>
<headline>Clinton transfers Hong Kong trade offices to China.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>In a procedural echo of the handover of Hong Kong from Britain to China, President Bill Clinton on Monday ordered the transfer of Hong Kong's trade offices in the United States to Chinese control.</p>
<p>That means that Hong Kong Economic and Trade Offices in the United States will have the same &quot;privileges, exemptions and immunities&quot; they enjoyed when they were under British control.</p>
<p>&quot;Previously, Hong Kong had trade offices in the United States under the auspices of Great Britain,&quot; a U.S. official said. &quot;This (executive order) keeps those offices open, but they're under Chinese auspices now.&quot;</p>
</text>
